{"id":"leetcode-834","version":1,"status":"approved","title":"Sum of Distances in Tree","summary":"Given an undirected connected tree with n nodes numbered from 0 to n-1 and n-1 edges, return an array of length n.","statement":"Given an undirected connected tree with n nodes numbered from 0 to n-1 and n-1 edges, return an array of length n. Each element in the array represents the sum of distances from the i-th node to all other nodes in the tree.","constraints":["n is 1 through 100,000, with nodes numbered zero through n-1.","edges contains exactly n-1 undirected edges forming one connected tree.","Return one distance sum per node in numeric node order."],"topics":["trees","graphs","depth first search","dynamic programming"],"prerequisites":["trees"],"signature":{"name":"sum_of_distances_in_tree","parameters":[{"name":"n","annotation":"int","adapter":"raw","source_parameter":null},{"name":"edges","annotation":"list[list[int]]","adapter":"raw","source_parameter":null}],"returns":"list[int]","return_adapter":"raw","node_policy":"values","result_mode":"return","mutated_parameter":null,"immutable_parameters":[]},"starter_code":"def sum_of_distances_in_tree(n: int, edges: list[list[int]]) -> list[int]:\n    # Write your solution here.\n    pass\n","reference_solution":"def sum_of_distances_in_tree(n, edges):\n    graph=[[] for _ in range(n)]\n    for left,right in edges:\n        graph[left].append(right)\n        graph[right].append(left)\n    parent=[-1]*n\n    parent[0]=0\n    order=[0]\n    for node in order:\n        for neighbor in graph[node]:\n            if neighbor!=parent[node]:\n                parent[neighbor]=node\n                order.append(neighbor)\n    subtree_size=[1]*n\n    answer=[0]*n\n    for node in reversed(order[1:]):\n        previous=parent[node]\n        subtree_size[previous]+=subtree_size[node]\n        answer[previous]+=answer[node]+subtree_size[node]\n    for node in order[1:]:\n        answer[node]=answer[parent[node]]+n-2*subtree_size[node]\n    return answer\n","brute_force_solution":null,"known_wrong_solutions":["def sum_of_distances_in_tree(n, edges):\n    graph=[[] for _ in range(n)]\n    for left,right in edges:\n        graph[left].append(right)\n        graph[right].append(left)\n    parent=[-1]*n\n    parent[0]=0\n    order=[0]\n    for node in order:\n        for neighbor in graph[node]:\n            if neighbor!=parent[node]:\n                parent[neighbor]=node\n                order.append(neighbor)\n    subtree_size=[1]*n\n    answer=[0]*n\n    for node in reversed(order[1:]):\n        previous=parent[node]\n        subtree_size[previous]+=subtree_size[node]\n        answer[previous]+=answer[node]+subtree_size[node]\n    for node in order[1:]:\n        answer[node]=answer[parent[node]]\n    return answer\n","def sum_of_distances_in_tree(n, edges):\n    graph=[[] for _ in range(n)]\n    for left,right in edges:\n        graph[left].append(right)\n        graph[right].append(left)\n    parent=[-1]*n\n    parent[0]=0\n    order=[0]\n    for node in order:\n        for neighbor in graph[node]:\n            if neighbor!=parent[node]:\n                parent[neighbor]=node\n                order.append(neighbor)\n    subtree_size=[1]*n\n    answer=[0]*n\n    for node in reversed(order[1:]):\n        previous=parent[node]\n        subtree_size[previous]+=subtree_size[node]\n        answer[previous]+=answer[node]+subtree_size[node]\n    for node in order[1:]:\n        answer[node]=answer[parent[node]]+n-subtree_size[node]\n    return answer\n"],"target_time_complexity":"O(n)","target_space_complexity":"O(n)","estimated_minutes":50,"rubric":{"algorithmic_insight":3,"prerequisites":2,"implementation":1,"performance_pressure":1,"edge_cases":1},"hints":["First compute every subtree size and the distance sum from node zero.","A bottom-up pass gives the root sum; a top-down pass can then move the root across each edge.","Moving into a child makes its subtree nodes one step closer and all other nodes one step farther: new = old + n - 2*subtree_size[child].","An iterative traversal avoids Python recursion depth limits on long chains; the two passes each visit every edge a constant number of times."],"editorial":"Build a parent-first traversal of the tree. Reverse it to accumulate subtree sizes and the sum of distances from node zero. For each parent-to-child edge, reroot: the child subtree becomes one edge closer while all remaining nodes become one edge farther. Thus answer[child] = answer[parent] + n - 2*subtree_size[child]. Both passes are linear and use no recursive call stack.","tests":[{"id":"lc-834-1","arguments":[6,[[0,1],[0,2],[2,3],[2,4],[2,5]]],"expected":[8,12,6,10,10,10],"comparator":"exact","visible":true,"explanation":"From node zero the distances are 0,1,1,2,2,2, summing to eight; rerooting gives [8,12,6,10,10,10].","expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-834-2","arguments":[3,[[0,1],[1,2]]],"expected":[3,2,3],"comparator":"exact","visible":true,"explanation":"The two endpoints each have distances 0,1,2 (sum three); the middle node has sum two.","expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-834-3","arguments":[1,[]],"expected":[0],"comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-834-4","arguments":[2,[[1,0]]],"expected":[1,1],"comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-834-5","arguments":[3,[[1,0],[2,0]]],"expected":[2,3,3],"comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-834-6","arguments":[4,[[1,0],[2,1],[3,2]]],"expected":[6,4,4,6],"comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-834-7","arguments":[4,[[1,0],[2,0],[3,0]]],"expected":[3,5,5,5],"comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-834-8","arguments":[5,[[1,0],[2,0],[3,1],[4,1]]],"expected":[6,5,9,8,8],"comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expe